{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1392184-spiritual-research","id":1392184,"title":"Spiritual research","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-28T07:04:21-07:00","id":1392184,"title":"Spiritual research","content":"For my Chronicle I am wanting to really develop The Shadow. But before I dive into and start making anything, I am wondering how well WoD: Book of Spirits hold up too MtAw 2e. And how well WtF 2e can be use for a source for Info about The Shadow with MtAw 2e. The last I am wondering bout (for the time being) is how much does The Shadow compare to oWoD Umbra? Mind you have have barely gotten into any info bout The Shadow so far, due to be relatively new to CoD lines.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: If there is topics on these things already on here, for give me for rehashing old topics. And please direct me to those threads. Thanks ahead of time for the info from all of y'all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","user":"Mahjemm01","date":". 05-28-2020, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T10:28:51-07:00","id":1392239,"title":"","content":"I recommend reading the posts by Papa Bear here:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/179059-what-does-the-shadow-look-like?_=1590685662866\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1590685662866</a><br /> <br /> They are some of the best descriptions of what the Shadow looks and feels like. I also recommend reading topics by Chris Allen (Acrozatarim) on the Werewolf the Forsaken forum, any one really, he fleshes out the Shadow and spirit aspects of the supernatural in a chillingly great way.<br /> <br /> The Shadow and Umbra are alien worlds, but feel very different. The Umbra is where the rules of reality start to have less hold, where you feel the echos and terror of unbound possibility. The Shadow is animistic and darwinistic, totemic and full of emotional extremes given form and want, but have a sideways logic binding it all together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-28-2020, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T10:41:30-07:00","id":1392242,"title":"","content":"Not to worried bout description bout it. I am more wondering if the Book of the Spirit can still be used with Second Edition content, with out having to convert most of the info in it. The threads in WtF is something I will look in to. And lastly....comparing oWoD Umbra, how does The Shadow compare? Is it the same thing just in a different IP? Or is there a significant difference between the two? I have a decade experience with oWoD Umbra. Does The Shadow have Realms like the Near Umbra does? Is The Shadow basically the Prenumbra? Is there a Deep Shadow that is analogous to the Deep Umbra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T11:10:27-07:00","id":1392264,"title":"","content":"Werewolf 2e will be a good reference for the Shadow which is compatible with Mage 2e.<br /> <br /> The Shadow is not the Umbra. For the most part it's one realm that corresponds to and reflects the nature of locations in the material realm, not a spectrum of shallower and deeper levels. (There are some places that exist in Shadow but not in the Material Realm, and the larger and more secret of these are sometimes referred to as &quot;deep&quot; places in the Shadow. But they're more like pockets than entrances into some other layer of Shadow, and they're rare exceptions.)<br /> <br /> The Astral Realms are more like what you're picturing, but are still not quite the Umbra. The Astral Realms do divide into successive layers of deeper submersion, with deeper layers of the Astral Realms reflecting more universal and cosmic expressions of the world-soul. But the &quot;shallower&quot; astral worlds aren't closer reflections of the Material Realm like the Penumbra would be. Instead the &quot;shallower&quot; astral worlds are more individual: one typically enters the internal world of a single person's soul, then can venture deeper into the collective unconscious of groups and humanity, and finally deeper into the world-soul of animals, plants and seemingly inanimate matter. Mages also typically don't travel to the Astral Realms like a spatial location, but meditate and project their soul-consciousness to awareness within them, while their body remains in the Material Realm, dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T12:50:12-07:00","id":1392283,"title":"","content":"I don't know much about the Umbra and the White Wolf wiki isn't very helpful. It appears that the Shadow resembles Penumbra as perceived by Garou, but without previous knowledge I can't say that for certain. The Shadow reflects not just Earth but also outer space, so the Deep Shadow isn't treated as a separate realm - it's just challenging to get there. Some things visit from there often - Sun and Moon Spirits, sent by Helios and Luna. Other things are not meant to breach Lunar orbit. If you want to know more about them, check &quot;Shunned by the Moon&quot; - a book of antagonists for Werewolf: the Forsaken. Also, check for Idigam - bizarre Spirits trapped on the Moon, some of whom escaped piggybacking on Apollo missions. They're described in &quot;Werewolf: the Forsaken 2nd Edition&quot; and &quot;Night Horrors - Wolfsbane&quot;. You can also search the Forums for examples, especially those posted by Acrozatarim. The term &quot;Deep Shadow&quot; exists also in Chronicles of Darkness, but refers to inaccessible parts of the Shadow. Little has been written about it.<br /> <br /> The nature of the Shadow remains unchanged between editions and gamelines. &quot;Book of Spirits&quot; describes it from a Mortal perspective and &quot;Predators&quot; (for Werewolf: the Forsaken) describes Spirits from Uratha perspective. &quot;Fallen Worlds&quot; for Mage: the Awakening has only ever been announced, so it doesn't count. Take note that some of Spirit mechanics are different between 1st and 2nd Edition, so you need to pay closer attention:<br /> <span style=\"color:#4D5156\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2022 </span></span></span></span>Bans were split into Bans and Banes.<br /> <span style=\"color:#4D5156\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2022 </span></span></span></span>Numina were split into Numina and Manifestations.<br /> <span style=\"color:#4D5156\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2022 </span></span></span>2nd Edition introduced Manifestation Conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T13:11:37-07:00","id":1392295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1392184-spiritual-research?p=1392264#post1392264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the most part it's one realm that corresponds to and reflects the nature of locations in the material realm</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much what the Umbra is in Werewolf the Apocalypse and Mage The Ascension......but the info about there isn't really any &quot;Near Umbra Realms&quot; analogous places is what I was wondering bout. Not really concerned bout the Astral Realm for the moment. Thanks for the info though. Have to admit kind of makes me sad that there isn't any Realms though. <br /> <br /> The info bout the Bans, Manifestations and such is the part that I was wanting to know. So.....basically....Book of Spirits would need some work to use it with the Second Edition line of games? Correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T13:25:04-07:00","id":1392297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1392184-spiritual-research?p=1392295#post1392295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The info bout the Bans, Manifestations and such is the part that I was wanting to know. So.....basically....Book of Spirits would need some work to use it with the Second Edition line of games? Correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. Bans and Banes will demand some creativity on your part. In 2nd Edition, every Spirit has a Ban (something that limits or controls their behavior), and a Bane (something that hurts them, even when intangible). In 1st Edition Spirits only had one or the other. Manifestations and related Conditions will require you to familiarize yourself with the rules - no way around it.<br /> <br /> Book of Spirits also has some Merits, cursed objects and miscellaneous mechanics, but you could probably use them without any changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T15:04:35-07:00","id":1392324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1392184-spiritual-research?p=1392295#post1392295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's pretty much what the Umbra is in Werewolf the Apocalypse and Mage The Ascension......but the info about there isn't really any &quot;Near Umbra Realms&quot; analogous places is what I was wondering bout. Not really concerned bout the Astral Realm for the moment. Thanks for the info though. Have to admit kind of makes me sad that there isn't any Realms though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shadow reflects the spiritual resonance of the Earthly area it corresponds to, typically more directly in places where the Gauntlet is thinner; this means the Shadow of human population centers tends to get a little weird compared to the faux-megafauna and scaled-up geography of the wilderness, with the artificial choirs taking a more organic cast to their features and an awful lot of Silent Hill-esque body-architecture.<br /> <br /> Places-That-Aren't are the aforementioned areas that lack material reflections, and they're often claimed as palaces and hideouts by more powerful spirits and their courts; the lack of direct correspondence with mundane reality allows them to get a little weirder than usual for a place where everything is alive and hungry and conceptually egocentric.<br /> <br /> The Shadow's also got a nebulous and poorly-understood connection to the deepest major layer of the Astral, the Dreaming Earth; werewolves experiencing particularly potent dreams project their consciousnesses there, unaware of and immune to the usual hazards of being in the raw manifestation of the world's soul, and the core of the Begotten's power ultimately hails from this root spiritual reality with a heavy layer of myth, legend, and nightmare connecting it to the human memescape.<br /> <br /> The dwelling of two of the Aeons in the deep depths of the Astral can notionally reach into the Dreaming Earth and out of the Astral frame of reference altogether to touch the Shadow; it's possible that one of them and/or some of their other &quot;siblings&quot; are responsible for giving birth to the Families of Horrors of Beast: the Primordial.<br /> <br /> On the opposite end of things, the historic destruction of an entire intervening border-world between the Shadow and the material sphere has produced a lot of long-lasting complications \u2014 Pangaeans, pillars of the world bridging flesh and spirit, were powerful manifestations of concepts like seasons and animals and geographic features, and of the ones that weren't completely killed off, most either gradually turning into spirits over centuries of time in the Shadow or dividing their forms and consciousnesses into countless pieces known as the Hosts to reunite and splinter and meddle with the world (especially the Gauntlet).<br /> <br /> Pangaeans were notable for a couple of things, not least being that they and the Aeons are the only two non-Supernal unAwakened beings with access to Arcana and they could all physically meditate themselves into the Astral on either side of the division between the human soul and the world-soul.<br /> <br /> Adding to all this, the way that ley lines and Hallows work connects loosely to the flow of Essence in the Shadow; ley lines produce consistent Resonance that affects the forms ephemera takes in the Shadow, forming complex nodes where they intersect, and powerful Hallows tend to exist along ley lines and conduct their Resonance as long as long as they're producing Mana (which they do as long as it's not allowed to accumulate to its limit as tass). These phenomena in turn sometimes serve as preconditions for the creation of a Supernal Verge, if not an Iris into Emanation Realms expressing particular Truths about an Arcanum (like Yggdrasil with Sacrifice [Spirit] or the Singularity with Progress [Time]).<br /> <br /> The thing to remember about the Shadow is that, while exceptions exist and ancient mages often treated unexplored individual locales as separate realms because the dimension is hostile territory, the Shadow is the spiritual reflection of the whole world, connected top-to-bottom and left-to-right in much the same way as mundane geography. Mages deal with a lot of stuff that's obscure even by supernatural standards, though, and nothing demonstrates that better than the wealth of other worlds their powers open up to them as tourists and interlopers; werewolves handle the Shadow as a place in a larger context that affects them because they have to live with it, but mere curiosity and personal circumstances are the more common reasons for a mage to deal with anything in another world, and Places-That-Aren't and other oddities beyond the quirks of Shadow ecology are very curious indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T20:49:56-07:00","id":1392408,"title":"","content":"Ok....going to be clear on this....I understand what the Shadow is. The purpose of the post was I was wondering if The Book of Spirits could be used without alot of conversion. Also if info bout The Shadow in WtF 2e could be used, as is, in MtAw 2e. And lastly....if The Shadow was a completely different beast from The Umbra found in WtA and MtA. And from what everyone has posted.....it's The Umbra. That simple. Minus having actual REALMS that The Umbra has. So far none of y'all have said anything at all that says that The Shadow is DIFFERENT then The Umbra of Werewolf The Apocalypse and Mage The Ascension. And I will go ahead and reinforce the statement that I have been a Storyteller for over a decade running Werewolf The Apocalypse and Mage The Ascension. Had a Chronicle set almost completely in The Umbra. I understand Ephemera, emotional resonance, Umbroods (spirit families), Blights, Wrymholes, Weaver Constructs. And so far....y'all have been talking bout those exact things, just used different jargon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T22:18:07-07:00","id":1392418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1392184-spiritual-research?p=1392408#post1392408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok....going to be clear on this....I understand what the Shadow is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay.<br /> <br /> Most of the information on the Shadow in general has remained the same for the last fifteen years and could be fit into the space of the five-page primers a given corebook's setting section accords it. Second Edition gamelines have not historically made supermassive changes in the way broadly-accessible parts of the cosmology operate, and the franchise's tack for supplements largely remains &quot;You won't need more than the corebook to be able to use the material presented in this book as-is.&quot;<br /> <br /> I've concerned myself almost exclusively with ChroD for the last ten years and had an ongoing deep-read of the entire franchise as a personal project for the last eight, which has combined with keeping up with other media to make familiarizing myself with the nuances of classic WoD lore beyond a quick wiki-dive extremely low-priority. The Umbra appears to simultaneously put a bunch of different types of world in the same basket and subdivide the spirit-based one into higher-intensity regions where the Shadow treats it all as a continuum of distortions that can get really weird, but I don't have the Apocalypse and Ascension materials to test that understanding.<br /> <br /> It's fine if you want to directly equate the spirit-world of one franchise with the spirit-world of its spiritual successor and all, but \u2014 well, no, it's not fine, we have enough of a problem with people thinking paradigms are relevant metaphysics here and otherwise confusing two distinct archetypes of wizard \u2014 but if you're going to do that when you've admitted to not having gotten through much of the book's information on the Shadow yet, it would be <i>great</i> to get some actual focused questions about what the difference is based on your understanding of the WoD stuff instead of assuming the old jargon carries the same weight with everyone else.<br /> <br /> Like, all you're doing here is rambling for a solid unbroken paragraph about how you know what the Shadow is without actually explaining if or how you expect it to be substantially different from the place that served the same function in Apocalypse and Ascension. I have no idea what \u2014 if any \u2014 degree of interconnection the High and Middle Umbra have with each other, but I can tell you how the Anima Mundi and the Shadow serve as weird divergent branches in how nonmaterial reality inhabited by things informed by nonhuman concepts manifests or point to the main ways that mages in Awakenings encounter a wide variety of &quot;realms&quot; that aren't just different neighborhoods in the Shadow of the Earth.<br /> <br /> It would be nice to get more than a blunt statement that sharing was a waste of my time out of that enthusiasm for this world that I'm particularly fond of. What's your understanding of the Umbra, besides that it has <span style=\"font-family:courier new\">REALMS</span>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T22:55:36-07:00","id":1392424,"title":"","content":"I mean, I'm pretty sure nobody in this thread has been talking about Blights or Weaver Constructs, because the Triat doesn't exist in CofD and the Shadow Realm doesn't have any analogous conflict. The other terms are good enough in terms of &quot;there is something analogous enough to this idea that it works as a point of comparison.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T23:34:30-07:00","id":1392426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1392184-spiritual-research?p=1392408#post1392408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok....going to be clear on this....I understand what the Shadow is. The purpose of the post was I was wondering if The Book of Spirits could be used without alot of conversion. Also if info bout The Shadow in WtF 2e could be used, as is, in MtAw 2e. And lastly....if The Shadow was a completely different beast from The Umbra found in WtA and MtA. And from what everyone has posted.....it's The Umbra. That simple. Minus having actual REALMS that The Umbra has. So far none of y'all have said anything at all that says that The Shadow is DIFFERENT then The Umbra of Werewolf The Apocalypse and Mage The Ascension. And I will go ahead and reinforce the statement that I have been a Storyteller for over a decade running Werewolf The Apocalypse and Mage The Ascension. Had a Chronicle set almost completely in The Umbra. I understand Ephemera, emotional resonance, Umbroods (spirit families), Blights, Wrymholes, Weaver Constructs. And so far....y'all have been talking bout those exact things, just used different jargon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Important differences (mostly from werewolf core book):<br /> -spirits continually try to eat each others<br /> -the sky is always cloudy, and sunrays impose additional force of gravity the more you go up<br /> -no more lunar bridge<br /> -maeljin spirits are similar to wyrm concept, but in a broad sense there isn t a dominant triatic force<br /> -spirits can use reaching manifestation to use powers on the other side of the gauntlet<br /> -caerns could broadly be translated into the loci, that are smaller, more abundant, and less &quot;holy ground&quot; for werewolf<br /> -gaian, as a major family of spirits doesn t exist, naturae spirits are not automatically friendly to werewolves<br /> -conversely, the oath of the moon don t say &quot;protect nature&quot; but &quot;patrol the gauntlet&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T02:50:45-07:00","id":1392462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1392184-spiritual-research?p=1392408#post1392408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok....going to be clear on this....I understand what the Shadow is. The purpose of the post was I was wondering if The Book of Spirits could be used without alot of conversion. Also if info bout The Shadow in WtF 2e could be used, as is, in MtAw 2e. And lastly....if The Shadow was a completely different beast from The Umbra found in WtA and MtA. And from what everyone has posted.....it's The Umbra. That simple. Minus having actual REALMS that The Umbra has. So far none of y'all have said anything at all that says that The Shadow is DIFFERENT then The Umbra of Werewolf The Apocalypse and Mage The Ascension. And I will go ahead and reinforce the statement that I have been a Storyteller for over a decade running Werewolf The Apocalypse and Mage The Ascension. Had a Chronicle set almost completely in The Umbra. I understand Ephemera, emotional resonance, Umbroods (spirit families), Blights, Wrymholes, Weaver Constructs. And so far....y'all have been talking bout those exact things, just used different jargon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thats them told..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T07:21:34-07:00","id":1392515,"title":"","content":"Neos01 thank you for that explanation for the main difference. That was one of the info that I have been wanting....the difference between The Umbra and The Shadow. I had notice the lack of the Trait in The Shadow. But with having just MtAw 2e, I didn't know the extent of the difference. I appreciate your info. <br /> <br /> Satchel, These Realms that I am speaking of is, essentially pocket dimensions that have formed form some abundance of a particular emotional resonance. Examples--Battlefield is a Realm formed from all the violence, anger, stress, the love of combat, etc, where it is literally a huge battlefield where knights on war horses wage war against Sherman tanks while F-14 Tomcats strafe the whole conflict. Pangaea is the Realm composed of the emotional resonance of Nature itself. A primordial jungle/forest where anklyasaurs fight off sabertooth tigers and herds of mammoths roam watching for T Rexs. Then there is The Scar, the result of modern pollution, fear, greed, Urban decay, and consumer consumption. Each Area has its own ...&quot;physics&quot;...laws if you will. And these are Realms found in what is called Near Umbra. As a traveller moves further from Earth in the Umbra, they approach which is analogous for Orbit and space. There a traveller encounters a sort of &quot;second gauntlet&quot; that separates the Near Umbra from the Deep Umbra. In the Deep Umbra, the Sol System planets in the Umbra have Realms themselves. The Deep Umbra is where things get extremely WEIRD and dangerous. To travel in the Deep Umbra, a traveller needs special abilities to just survive and keep moving. Travel in the Deep Umbra is the WoD &quot;high level&quot; version of the game. Werewolves and Mages that go there need abilities only gained after a hundred or more experience points. The whole time all Realms, Near and Deep Umbra, are flavored by one of three key traits. These traits, called Triat, is the expression of Dynamic (The Wyld), Static (The Weaver) or Entropy (The Wyrm). But there is a problem with The Triat. The Wyrm, Entropy, has gone off the rails. Gone batshit crazy. The Weaver, in it's quest to impose order and structure everything, has caused The Wyrm to be caught in The Weaver's webbing. Now The Wyrm is corrupted and lashing out, and has become a nightmare looking to destroy everything. <br /> <br /> These Realms allow WtA and MtA to take their modern setting game and make stories of fantasy and even science fiction and then go right back to modern setting. And it's these Realms that I have been referring to and wondering if they exist in The Shadow. Because frankly, those things is one of my favorite aspects of both WtA and MtA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T08:06:41-07:00","id":1392536,"title":"","content":"None of the realms you described appear in the Shadow. All of them would, however, fit in the Astral Realms (with the Near Umbral realms being mostly Temenotic realms, and the Far Umbral realms being parts of the Anima Mundi). I also happen to know that there's a part of the Umbra (don't know if it's Near or Far or something else) that is a lot closer to the Underworld in CofD.<br /> The Shadow is a (somewhat distorted) reflection of the physical world. Not a reflection of every concept that may appear in the physical world; but the physical world itself.*<br /> Many spirits <i>do</i> reflect more abstract concepts (emotions being quite common anywhere humans gather), but they are all always spirits first with their nature (what concept they reflect) being their &quot;flavour&quot;. A spirit of fire, a spirit of serenity, and a spirit of hedgehogs will have quite different personalities, but they will all be spirits and share the same base drive of wanting Essence (which they either gain from sources of their nature, like a monk being serene or a hedgehog, or by hunting compatible spirits to gain their Essence). To this purpose they may try to influence the physical world to gain additional lr stronger sources of Essence. The spirit of serenity might induce calmness (quite possibly to the point of apathy) in people, the spirit of fire will fuel fires or start new ones, and the spirit of hedgehogs might bind itself to a hedgehog to ensure a steady supply of Essence while constantly being close enough to protect it (or just straight up Claim it, creating a physical and mutated spirit-hedgehog fusion horror). This is generally what the player faction of werewolves try to prevent (though there are many other threats as well).<br /> <br /> *With a few exceptions, but they tend to be somewhat rare and special in their own way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-29-2020, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T08:13:15-07:00","id":1392540,"title":"","content":"There could be Places that Aren\u2019t in the Shadow that are representative of a giant battlefield or something, but it\u2019s going to still follow the rules of Shadow instead of having new rules for new modes of existence. It could also exist separately and simultaneously in the Underworld and Astral and would still play by the rules of those realms.<br /> <br /> For new rules/modes of existence you would probably need to go to an Emanation realm. Which is a category of other world completely separate from the ones I mentioned though they can have pathways that connect them.<br /> <br /> There definitely isn\u2019t a deep umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T09:29:23-07:00","id":1392572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1392184-spiritual-research?p=1392540#post1392540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There could be Places that Aren\u2019t in the Shadow that are representative of a giant battlefield or something, but it\u2019s going to still follow the rules of Shadow instead of having new rules for new modes of existence. It could also exist separately and simultaneously in the Underworld and Astral and would still play by the rules of those realms.<br /> <br /> For new rules/modes of existence you would probably need to go to an Emanation realm. Which is a category of other world completely separate from the ones I mentioned though they can have pathways that connect them.<br /> <br /> There definitely isn\u2019t a deep umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank Mrmdubiois, that info was something else I was wondering bout.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T12:46:14-07:00","id":1393491,"title":"","content":"Most everything that was on the spectrum of Umbra from higher to lower has a corresponding set of rules. Whereas there was basically a single axis of weirdness in oWoD, (lower would be negative. Deep umbra would simply be farther. Both fall on the same axis) there are multiple axes in CoD.<br /> <br /> The lower, near Umbra is ghostly Twilight. The lower umbra is the Underworld... and, arguably, some of the Lower Depths.<br /> <br /> The upper near umbra splits into the Inner Realms (Astral) and the Spirit. The near side Twilight for these things is distinct in 2e (and, arguably in 1e) but there are increasing depths to most of these axes, as well.<br /> <br /> The Twilight of mental projections extends into the dreams of individuals and then into the dreams of groups and the world. There are many distinct realms in there and you will likely find much of what you expect from the deep umbra in there. The axis is towards a more universal soul... and, ultimately, reaches to the Supernal Realms through the Abyss.<br /> <br /> Spirits have realms that are linked to physical reality and then stretch off into more esoteric forms.(Can't find my Book of the Spirits, just now, so I can't skim it to spot things that jump out as incompatible, but the vast majority of the fluff is basically applicable.)<br /> <br /> The really out-there deep umbra stuff is Abyssal or Lower Depths... or even Emanation Realms and the Supernal.<br /> <hr /><br /> If weird, deep umbra quests are something you enjoy, Stupid Loserman nailed it: The Astral Realms are probably what you seek, so the Book of Spiriits may not be of great value. There's a reason Awakening recast the Dreamspeakers as a Mind legacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T02:58:44-07:00","id":1394005,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Mahjemm01;n1392242]Not to worried bout description bout it. I am more wondering if the Book of the Spirit can still be used with Second Edition content, with out having to convert most of the info in it. /QUOTE]<br /> <br /> I am using characters and concepts from that book in my current game and it works pretty well. You might need to fiddle with certain Numina or other mechanical widgets to make them jive with 2nd editions rules but all the concepts and inspiration work just fine so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T14:22:25-07:00","id":1394150,"title":"","content":"When you say &quot;fiddle&quot; lol, how much work are we talking bout? If it's really barely thing at all then great. But if it's a real break mechanics down and then rebuild, I'll have to pass. <br /> <br /> Hoping to have the Fallen Worlds as a major thing in my Chronicle at one point. Being a long time ST for the old WoD one of the things I loved about the Umbra was the possibility to have a adventure where the players can go have a High Fantasy story with dragons, and griffons and all and then next adventure they are solving a murder in the modern city and have them fight the BBG on a moving roller coaster. Wanting that kind of diversity for my Mage game. But before I started homebrewing things I wanted to see if those things was already available in the game thru canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T15:00:58-07:00","id":1394156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1392184-spiritual-research?p=1394150#post1394150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being a long time ST for the old WoD one of the things I loved about the Umbra was the possibility to have a adventure where the players can go have a High Fantasy story with dragons, and griffons and all and then next adventure they are solving a murder in the modern city and have them fight the BBG on a moving roller coaster. Wanting that kind of diversity for my Mage game. But before I started homebrewing things I wanted to see if those things was already available in the game thru canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Astral, specifically the Temenos, provides much of this, barring some extra stipulations about what counts for what. Your spells all can do better when they're playing to the themes and aesthetics of the realm they're in, and your actions can have some impact on mortal culture without necessary having to explain why your cabal's big loud finale didn't rip the skin off of every witness's face and summon an eldritch horror through their lack of gnostic insight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T15:10:57-07:00","id":1394158,"title":"","content":"None of that is really part of the Shadow*. You should really look up the Astral Realms if you haven't already. Basically everything you've described from the Umbra would fit so much better in the Astral rather than in the Shadow. The Astral is much more of a successor to the Umbra (especially those parts of the Umbra explored in MtAsc) than the Shadow. The Astral Realms book still works great despite being 1e. A few of the mechanics are outdated but it's the setting information that is the most interesting parts and afaik it's still 100% canon.<br /> <br /> *Except for the modern city; but you won't have a murder mystery play out there because it's populated by spirits and spirits wouldn't care if another spirit dies unless it upsets the power dynamics in the area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T15:14:51-07:00","id":1394160,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you want the Astral Realms for that, that's both the signature otherworld for mages and the place where different conceptual realms manifest genre-specific phenomena to suit the ideas the realm embodies. The first edition Astral Realms supplement still has a lot of relevant and useful setting detail for plotting a 2e astral-heavy game, though any mechanical widgets or astral entity (what Mage 2e calls goetia) writeups would need to be rebuilt for 2e. But it's great for context and guides, it fits exactly in with how 2e describes the Astral Realms, and its sample astral environments that receive multiple-page writeups include &quot;the planet Mars as a place of war, as imagined through pulp science fiction, with green men wielding swords and rayguns,&quot; and &quot;the ruins of lost civilizations of intelligent awakened housecats or crows, which rose and fell entirely in the world of dreams, purely possible but never tangibly realized.&quot;<br /> <br /> While Mind is the relevant Arcanum for spells which directly transform or manipulate the nature of goetic beings, it's not really necessary for a mage who just wants to project into the astral and go adventuring in the collective unconscious to uncover secrets, chase troublemakers, or influence ideas. The Spirit Arcanum, meanwhile, while important if you want to try to reach into the Shadow Realm, is generally more practical as a means of influencing latent spirits to achieve results in the material realm (which may or may not involve directly transforming or manipulating the nature of those spirits as the means to do so).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T15:18:43-07:00","id":1394161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1392184-spiritual-research?p=1394150#post1394150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being a long time ST for the old WoD one of the things I loved about the Umbra was the possibility to have a adventure where the players can go have a High Fantasy story with dragons, and griffons and all and then next adventure they are solving a murder in the modern city and have them fight the BBG on a moving roller coaster. Wanting that kind of diversity for my Mage game. But before I started homebrewing things I wanted to see if those things was already available in the game thru canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to the Astral, there's also the Hedge (from <i>Changeling: the Lost</i>) that has plenty of its own weirdness and a distinctly fairy-tale horror to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T09:32:11-07:00","id":1394373,"title":"","content":"Speaking of The Hedge, Proindrakenzol, I have a copy of CtL 2e because I am wanting to have adventures in the Hedge. But I have read that ...idrc...where exactly....The Hedge flays non Changeling and Fae souls while travelling through it. I will admit that I honestly don't know if that would happen to a Mage, and if so, is there a defense against that for the Mage. I have done some Googling on the subject but have yet to find a definitive answer for that. I do know that I could go with the old Golden Rule--its my game and do what I feel fits and goes with what I want my game to be. Though if there is concert answer for it though I would like to read up on it and see how exactly I want to put it in my game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T11:00:33-07:00","id":1394397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1392184-spiritual-research?p=1394373#post1394373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of The Hedge, Proindrakenzol, I have a copy of CtL 2e because I am wanting to have adventures in the Hedge. But I have read that ...idrc...where exactly....The Hedge flays non Changeling and Fae souls while travelling through it. I will admit that I honestly don't know if that would happen to a Mage, and if so, is there a defense against that for the Mage. I have done some Googling on the subject but have yet to find a definitive answer for that. I do know that I could go with the old Golden Rule--its my game and do what I feel fits and goes with what I want my game to be. Though if there is concert answer for it though I would like to read up on it and see how exactly I want to put it in my game.</div> </div> </div> </div>The hedge-soul-flaying thing was in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T12:09:13-07:00","id":1394404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1392184-spiritual-research?p=1394373#post1394373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of The Hedge, Proindrakenzol, I have a copy of CtL 2e because I am wanting to have adventures in the Hedge. But I have read that ...idrc...where exactly....The Hedge flays non Changeling and Fae souls while travelling through it.</div> </div> </div> </div>1e's version of the Hedge had it so that most non-changelings deferred rolls to lose their Morality stats until they left the Hedge, and wandering through the Thorns/leaving the path stripped dots from Morality and Wisdom outright every hour that a character spent wandering; mechanically, this runs the same risks as soul loss for mages, including losing the ability to cast once they bottom out.<br /> <br /> Since Integrity stats work so differently in 2e, this is less of a concern than the fact that &quot;the Thorns&quot; means &quot;the parts of the Hedge that are particularly dangerous.&quot; Navigating the Hedge in the Thorns is tricky \u2014 it's &quot;faster&quot; in the chase that models navigation (you practically need a vehicle or a lot of Speed boosts to have a shorter run to success than the Hedge itself), it rolls more dice in the pursuit, and any Hedgespinning rolls it makes in response to the characters' actions gets the 8-Again rule for generating successes to spend creating complications, to say nothing of the higher likelihood that you are in an <i>actively</i> dangerous environment \u2014 and just not being fae makes the process of navigating the Hedge in general harder (there's no Wyrd rating to reduce the number of successes you need directly, the Hedge doesn't subtract anyone's Clarity from its effective Initiative, and mental/emotional Conditions further affect the Hedge's ability to get you lost by winning the chase).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T14:06:04-07:00","id":1394430,"title":"","content":"So, please correct and explain if I got this wrong....they done away soul flaying of Thorns and instead increased the likelyhood of those without Wyrd getting hopelessly lost in the Hedge and winding up in the dangerous &quot;wild&quot; parts now called Thorns? I haven't been reading my copy of CtL 2e, YET.<br /> <br /> And to bring this back to being a Mage thread lol. What's the best sources to read up on the Lower Depths? I do own Summoners, Left Hand Path, and I believe Imperial Mysteries (have to check my library when I get home). Like CtL, I haven't read those YET. And do you all think a adventure could be set in the Lower Depths? And if so, would it be (preferably) a &quot;high level&quot; Story?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","user":"Mahjemm01","date":". 06-05-2020, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T14:28:19-07:00","id":1394436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1392184-spiritual-research?p=1394430#post1394430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, please correct and explain if I got this wrong....they done away soul flaying of Thorns and instead increased the likelyhood of those without Wyrd getting hopelessly lost in the Hedge and winding up in the dangerous &quot;wild&quot; parts now called Thorns? I haven't been reading my copy of CtL 2e, YET.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Thorns were in 1e as well, it's just that the division of Hedge-type went from &quot;consistent path,&quot; &quot;on the path,&quot; &quot;off the path,&quot; &quot;far off the path&quot; to &quot;consistent path,&quot; &quot;most other places,&quot; &quot;this is where the Big Bad Wolf lives.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's no longer a delay on breaking points and their equivalent and it no longer directly removes dots from the relevant Traits, but the Hedge is set up in such a manner that if it gets what it wants before you do, you're going to get funneled into the Thorns or the front door of Arcadia; Hedgespinning allows its users (including the Hedge) to force other characters' failures to become dramatic failures, dramatic failures in the Thorns result in really bad-news Conditions like Lost or Madness, and negative Conditions tend to play out in the environment in metaphors that tend to incur further breaking points.<br /> <br /> And all this is to say nothing of the fact that one of the easier ways to get anywhere in the Hedge is to accept the guidance of a hobgoblin in exchange for Goblin Debt \u2014 a meter that only changelings can reduce without doing favors for the goblins they owe instead of letting it build up to the level of &quot;you're a hobgoblin now, too, have fun sticking to the Hedge until you've worked off your Debt.&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically, though, yes, the principal issue has changed the precise flavor of &quot;you will likely wind up trapped in slavery after long enough&quot; that being stuck in the Hedge long-term promises the incautious wanderer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And to bring this back to being a Mage thread lol. What's the best sources to read up on the Lower Depths? I do own Summoners, Left Hand Path, and I believe Imperial Mysteries (have to check my library when I get home). Like CtL, I haven't read those YET. And do you all think a adventure could be set in the Lower Depths? And if so, would it be (preferably) a &quot;high level&quot; Story? </div> </div> </div>World of Darkness: Inferno provides some information on the most consistent-ish denizens of Abaddon, and Werewolf's treatment on Wounds and the Maeljin can be used fairly well conceptually, but the Lower Depths are you're-not-coming-back territory for most games. Phenomena emerging &quot;upward&quot; <i>from</i> the Depths cause a great deal of trouble on their own, usually, because the world's not built for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T19:13:23-07:00","id":1394476,"title":"","content":"Wounds and Maejlin sound very similar to WtA Blights--a spiritually area of the Penumbra that has been corrupted and defiled, and Malfaes--a Deep Umbra Realm that is a Spirit Hell that is ruled over by Maeljins--Incarna Spirits of various forms of Defilement and Corruption. Wrymholes are direct paths to Maelfas. <br /> <br /> And going back to the Hedge, but trying to keep it Mage lol.....is there a way that a Mage can protect himself from the Debt or navigate the Hedge himself? For example, will Fate Arcanum help with that? Or Prime even? Or is that something that will problem addressed in Contagion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T21:00:24-07:00","id":1394496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1392184-spiritual-research?p=1394476#post1394476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wounds and Maejlin sound very similar to WtA Blights--a spiritually area of the Penumbra that has been corrupted and defiled, and Malfaes--a Deep Umbra Realm that is a Spirit Hell that is ruled over by Maeljins--Incarna Spirits of various forms of Defilement and Corruption. Wrymholes are direct paths to Maelfas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't surprise me.<br /> <br /> The short version: Inferno covers demons who sort of operate by treating the material world the way archmages treat the Supernal \u2014 as a more-&quot;real&quot; source of power and influence whose inhabitants can be leveraged to grow.<br /> <br /> Every Infernal demon can Fall to Whispers, effectively becoming a Rank 0 parasitic thoughtform encouraging its human(/like) host to commit evil deeds and create or amend the demon's written description for greater power; some demons start out as Diaboli \u2014 corrupted ghosts, spirits, or goetia \u2014 though past a certain point it becomes unlikely they won't have progressed to the true demonic state of a Dominion.<br /> <br /> Dominions who used to be Immundi (corrupted spirits) make up the bulk of the loose category of true demons who shift the world toward sin by interfering with its material conditions \u2014 the way they push people to do evil is mostly by <i>making the world a worse place to live in</i> so that it's easier to abandon compassion and do things you know are harmful and wrong.<br /> <br /> For Inferno's purposes, the Maeljin are particularly powerful true demons; in Werewolf, their modus operandi is to empower agents from deep within the Wounds formed by atrocity and overwhelming negative resonance, which jives with the Lower Depths' main tactics of draining things out of the world and/or turning natives of reality into ways of draining things out of the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And going back to the Hedge, but trying to keep it Mage lol.....is there a way that a Mage can protect himself from the Debt </div> </div> </div>By not making deals with goblins. The only other regular source of it is from Goblin Contracts, which non-fae can't get without a stint as a hobgoblin.<br /> <br /> You might make an argument for allowing the Unbound Fate Attainment to let you try and shrug off incurring Goblin Debt, but since it's an abstraction of the broader phenomenon of &quot;this is a paid service, however that manifests,&quot; it's hard to invoke it under any rationale besides potentially eventually becoming a hobgoblin constituting an alteration of your destiny \u2014you're generally not tricked into it so much as offered the bargain under duress.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or navigate the Hedge himself? For example, will Fate Arcanum help with that? Or Prime even? Or is that something that will problem addressed in Contagion? </div> </div> </div>It's literally just handled with regular Chase mechanics, except that even without another person-scale participant the Hedge counts as a sort of loose time-limit, and also navigating the Hedge or otherwise interacting with it can prompt sudden changes to your surroundings.<br /> <br /> In general, if you're not a changeling then your best bet for moving quickly through the Hedge is \u2014 surprise! \u2014 <i>stay on the path</i>. The Hedge is &quot;slower&quot; on trods, especially powerful ones, and its Hedgespinning is most hampered on the main roads, where its consistent pool of eight dice doesn't get the 10-Again quality (it gets 8-Again in the Thorns and 9-Again everywhere else, and this is a roll that specifically requires it to get more than one success to accomplish anything). The old warnings get passed along for a reason.<br /> <br /> <i>Without</i> fae-specific advantages, your best bet for navigating the Hedge as a mage is going to be anything that makes winning a Chase easier \u2014 high Skills and Attributes, high Speed and Initiative, the ability to quickly gather information about your route and surroundings, and so on. Above all else, <i>move quickly</i> \u2014 the Hedge's dice pool for counter-navigating gets bigger with every turn of the chase.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T23:54:02-07:00","id":1394509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1392184-spiritual-research?p=1394476#post1394476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wounds and Maejlin sound very similar to WtA Blights--a spiritually area of the Penumbra that has been corrupted and defiled, and Malfaes--a Deep Umbra Realm that is a Spirit Hell that is ruled over by Maeljins--Incarna Spirits of various forms of Defilement and Corruption. Wrymholes are direct paths to Maelfas.<br /> <br /> And going back to the Hedge, but trying to keep it Mage lol.....is there a way that a Mage can protect himself from the Debt or navigate the Hedge himself? For example, will Fate Arcanum help with that? Or Prime even? Or is that something that will problem addressed in Contagion?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, Wounds are essentially Blights. Edited that out and apparently forgot to edit it back into my post. Maeljin were <i>obviously </i>expies of those particular Wyrmspawn in WtF 1e.<br /> <br /> <br /> As to ways of dealing with fey things:<br /> <br /> In 1e, a mage with Fate 3 (IIRC) could use mana to create and use Glamour. (There were rules for most interactions established, actually, though some were better than others. At least it wasn't &quot;No.&quot;)<br /> <br /> 2e hasn't, to my knowledge, mentioned making Glamour, but Prime 1's <i>Word of Command</i> + Fate 1 can trigger things like gateways and tokens. Fate can manipulate an oath. Space 1's <i>Correspondence</i> can be used to identify a Key.<br /> <br /> Space is really good for navigation, in general, it bears noting. <i>Ground Eater</i> would be quite helpful in Hedge chases. <i>Ban</i> could be mighty useful with Fate to keep out naughty things. (perhaps naughty things like Hedgespinning in general. Surely a <i>Pocket Dimension</i> should provide some respite.)<br /> <br /> An argument can be made that <i>Chaos Mastery</i> and <i>Strings of Fate</i> (Fate 4) both serve as a means of manipulating the Hedge in a manner similar to Hedgespinning. The <i>Unbound Fate</i> Attainment would certainly apply versus <b>some</b> Hedgespinning.<br /> <br /> Depending on how you are interpreting &quot;location&quot; in the Hedge, <i>Teleport</i> or <i>Co-Location</i> hold some merit. <br /> <br /> Any magic that resists a hazard of the form spun would work against it, too, it bears noting. Thus, there probably shouldn't be a &quot;shield vs. all Hedgespun attacks&quot; under any Arcana. Protection from <i>being</i> Hedgespun, on the other hand, sounds reasonable for Fate 2. <i>Control Heat</i> could be brought to bear against a blaze. <i>Ban</i> could provide shelter from a wide array of things with proper Arcana backing it up.<br /> <br /> Biggest crossover headache is figuring out how to apply Withstand ratings versus Clash of Wills. In most cases, I suspect a Clash wouldn't apply because both effects occur, regardless. If the mage has some spell for locating something or navigating without fail, the Hedge should have some sort of Clash of Wills against that effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T04:17:30-07:00","id":1394535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1392184-spiritual-research?p=1394509#post1394509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Biggest crossover headache is figuring out how to apply Withstand ratings versus Clash of Wills. In most cases, I suspect a Clash wouldn't apply because both effects occur, regardless. If the mage has some spell for locating something or navigating without fail, the Hedge should have some sort of Clash of Wills against that effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clash of Wills are for mutually exclusive supernatural powers. If the Hedge itself provides resistance against anything it would do so through an added Withstand rating.<br /> <br /> Shielding spells vs Hedgespun attacks by others grants a CoW like most or Shielding spells unless the nature of the spell and the attack means the spell should auto-succeed. I believe the latter is more common since CoW Shielding spells mostly apply against supernatural powers used directly against you, and Hedgespinning is more about shaping the environment to cause relatively mundane attacks.<br /> Shielding spells don't use Withstand ratings as part of their protection (unless they protect against other spells, in which case they add one instead of having to overcome one).<br /> <br /> Also, don't forget Mage Armour, which works likes usual.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's a few additional rules for how Mage magic interacts with the Hedge, Goblins and Changeling Contracts in one of the new eras in Dark Eras 2. Can't remember which one, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T07:10:05-07:00","id":1394552,"title":"","content":"Have been toying with the idea of getting WoD:Infernal, but it being 1e content I have been concerned that it wouldn't &quot;mesh.&quot; I am now guessing it is bout like Book of Spirits with how well it works with 2e content. I have always enjoyed the concept of Infernal in a WoD (oWod and nWod), and that it was even more &quot;evil&quot; then the regular &quot;bad guys.&quot; <br /> <br /> All the feed back on the Hedge and CtL is has been a huge boon. I appreciate all of ya'll taking the time and educate me on that particular subject. The idea of having a &quot;Guillermo Del Toro Hellboy&quot; aspect for a Mage game intrigues me. Now I am wondering if a Gentry could be actually summoned and Boons gained from it(Contracts?)? And if so how would a mage go about doing that? I imagine that a Mage would need the Gentry's True Name to do it(unless of course Gentry don't have True Names).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T07:32:11-07:00","id":1394560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1392184-spiritual-research?p=1394552#post1394552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I am wondering if a Gentry could be actually summoned and Boons gained from it(Contracts?)</div> </div> </div> </div>They're above the pay-grade of mages to summon in any fashion that isn't equally accessible (and dangerous) to everybody else; the Faerie Favor Merit represents one of the safer methods, but otherwise you're going to have to catch the attention of a god and convince it by hook or by crook to give you lent access to things it owns and try not to get screwed over by the fine print. You generally have to get them over a barrel so that they'll offer you something to get out of it, which means a fair bit of legwork learning what oaths and bargains it's sworn with whom.<br /> <br /> The Gentry have Names behind their Titles, but their main uses are to changelings using Contracts or others attempting to physically harm it; if knowing it lets you summon a Stranger, it's because that particular Stranger has an agreement or frailty that compels it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T14:30:25-07:00","id":1394627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1392184-spiritual-research?p=1394552#post1394552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Now I am wondering if a Gentry could be actually summoned and Boons gained from it(Contracts?)? And if so how would a mage go about doing that? I imagine that a Mage would need the Gentry's True Name to do it(unless of course Gentry don't have True Names).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It would be a customized thing if you do it. Fate might well be able to impose such a thing on some of the Others, but given their only partially real nature and largely optional interactions with Time, that &quot;being&quot; might not even exist at any given moment to be summoned. Still, a Fate Master might well be able to edit the story of a Title.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Changeling: The Lost Second Edition, p267</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A True Fae is not a person, but a Name wrapped in a tapestry of vows and deals. Deep in the mists of forgotten time, the Fae bargained with Arcadia itself, declaring that they would exist \u2014 that they would own the land entire and claim it as a vessel for their Wyrd, dreams, and facets, in exchange for a web of arcane rules so complex no one of them could ever know them all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> edit: Dang. Somehow it lost almost all of my edits when it first posted. I looked up the terminology and had a second relevant quote... Fah. Not worth rewriting.<br /> <br /> Short form: Titles should automatically win a Clash of Wills over something related to its purview. If the change falls in line with its nature but not its purview, it's fair game. Adding a vulnerability to summoning would be fair for many Titles, but that vulnerability would express as one of the Title's (normally negotiated) weaknesses. You could also rule that a form of summoning was, in fact, a part of Titles by universal nature as one of the esoteric agreements that they made. Fey being what they are, there should be some sort of special requirement per Title, roughly equivalent to learning their name, as setting up puzzles is fun and being at mortal beck and call wouldn't be. <br /> <br /> I don't think True Names should really be valid targets for this sort of editing at all but <b>certainly</b> not unless known/fully revealed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 06-09-2020, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T04:31:38-07:00","id":1394752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1392184-spiritual-research?p=1394627#post1394627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It would be a customized thing if you do it. Fate might well be able to impose such a thing on some of the Others, but given their only partially real nature and largely optional interactions with Time, that &quot;being&quot; might not even exist at any given moment to be summoned. Still, a Fate Master might well be able to edit the story of... I've forgotten the terms.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this but put stipulations, like it doesn't work on True Fae in Arcadia or even the Hedge, only those reduced so lowly forms as they already appear in the mortal world, basically only those already banished from such places and stalk the material world of humanity. So not only would you need to know the True Name of a Gentry but that Gentry would need to be one of the very rare ones banished from the Fae realms. But as beings of time and fate if you meet those catches and call them just right I am sure their own Wyrd would make them show up, and you may find your own Fate Magic starting to obey rules the True Fae understand and you don't. This would be a GREAT time to explore the consequences of the themes of Hubris people tend to forget to include in their Mage stories when they are thinking up their ill-conceived power fantasies.<br /> <br /> Hey the Fate Arcanum itself says if you don't respect it that it isn't just Paradox that'll start to work against you but the weave of Fate itself, don't get much more disrespectful than disrespecting the Narrative Journey of a literal Avatar of Fate. I'd have some spontaneous <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/475-wyrd-sorcery\">Wyrd Sorcery</a> automatically succeed on the mage with the Doom of the Tale being &quot;the Mage suffers a cost for whatever he hoped to gain from the True Fae Seven Fold what it is worth and learn to never try to summon even the weakest of the Gentry.&quot; (Possible twist later is truncating the Doom to the second half if the Mage takes the lesson to heart so well they caution others with their story) If I was feeling in the &quot;REALLY!? This fool player never heard of <i>careful-what-you-wish-for</i> allegories? Alright then, time for that tale&quot; mood then the a note from the True Fae appears from the Future (at least it's from the Future according the Mage Sight and the Time Arcanum even though that isn't possible unless the Mage is in the Past -according to how mages believe times work- and the mage is in the present) right before they cast granting them what they want with a warning to be careful what they wish for as it may cost them more than they know.<br /> Also all fate Magic against this particular Wyrd Sorcery just makes things worse, because of course it does. This goes up there with the &quot;oh I am so smart I would totally outsmart the Genie of that story&quot; feeling most of us role players have, as if litigiousness was a bulwark to narrative flow of destiny, it isn't. Destiny is destiny because its the weight of <i>how things work</i> pressing <i>how things are</i> through the mesh of the weave of <i>everything that has come before</i>. Fate is the shape of what comes out the other side of this collection of pressures shaping events.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heraclitus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#008080\"><i>(moral)</i></span> Character is Destiny</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wikipedia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_English\" target=\"_blank\">Old English</a><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> term </span></span></span><i>wyrd</i><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> derives from a </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_Germanic\" target=\"_blank\">Common Germanic</a><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> term </span></span></span><i>*wur\u0111\u00edz</i><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">.</span></span></span><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wyrd#cite_note-1\" target=\"_blank\">[1]</a></sup><i>Wyrd</i><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> has cognates in </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Saxon\" target=\"_blank\">Old Saxon</a><i>wurd</i><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">,</span></span></span><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wyrd#cite_note-2\" target=\"_blank\">[2]</a></sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_High_German\" target=\"_blank\">Old High German</a><i>wurt</i><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">,</span></span></span><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wyrd#cite_note-3\" target=\"_blank\">[3]</a></sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Norse\" target=\"_blank\">Old Norse</a><i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ur%C3%B0r\" target=\"_blank\">ur\u00f0r</a></i><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, Dutch </span></span></span><i>worden</i><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> (to become), and German </span></span></span><i>werden</i><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">. The </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proto-Indo-European_root\" target=\"_blank\">Proto-Indo-European root</a><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> is </span></span></span><i>*wert-</i><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> &quot;to turn, rotate&quot;, in </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_Germanic\" target=\"_blank\">Common Germanic</a><i>*wir\u00fe-</i><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> with a meaning &quot;to come to pass, to become, to be due&quot; (also in </span></span></span><i><a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weor%C3%BE\" target=\"_blank\">weor\u00fe</a></i><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, the notion of &quot;origin&quot; or &quot;</span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worth\" target=\"_blank\">worth</a><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot; both in the sense of &quot;connotation, price, value&quot; and &quot;affiliation, identity, esteem, honour and dignity)</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>By this particular type of Hubris and comparing it to classical tales, especially with all warnings in folklore about the fair folk which would only fail to be headed by the likes of teen ignoring the harbinger in a slasher flick (ie <i>Cabin in The Woods</i>) and trope it is more than fair to say any Mage is basically telling Fate itself they are opting-in to be a Cautionary Tale rather than the Power Fantasy which mages whom respect Fate opt-into.<br /> <br /> Why use mechanics from the forum? Because mage characters are not mage players and that mage players read the book and understand the actual mechanics behind the world takes some of the mystery out of it for them. Also It is well written and you don't need to know changeling to implement it, just a good narrative sense and the post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-07-2020, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T11:47:11-07:00","id":1394833,"title":"","content":"A lot of good information there and a mine for delving for stories. Can be used for several different themes and moods. I, for one, look at the mechanics as a frame work. Something to keep the story within so that it doesn't get to &quot;out there and wild.&quot; The narrative is body, but the mechanics are the bones. Keeps a consistency within the world I building. <br /> <br /> Now with this all being said, let's look at Huntsmen. Would Huntsmen fall in the same category as Gentry--if it makes a good narrative to allow one to be summoned, then allow it. Or would it be easier to summon a Huntsman? And could a Mage gain something from doing it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T18:22:29-07:00","id":1394923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1392184-spiritual-research?p=1394833#post1394833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now with this all being said, let's look at Huntsmen. Would Huntsmen fall in the same category as Gentry--if it makes a good narrative to allow one to be summoned, then allow it. Or would it be easier to summon a Huntsman? And could a Mage gain something from doing it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Huntsmen are generally categorized as either dwelling in Old Arcadia, well beyond casual access, or arriving on Earth to get something for the Stranger that's cut out its heart and poured a Title in, which gets a bonus to resist attempts to make it disobey its orders. Like with the Gentry, there's no means of summoning them that doesn't rely on an established relationship where you've already met.<br /> <br /> There is <i>basically nothing</i> a Huntsman specifically can offer a mage who is not specifically looking for a way to fuck up a changeling's life, because what they're for is &quot;the Fae can send a type of antagonist after you that can stalk you and mess with your head and doesn't have the downsides of other fae threats.&quot; A given specimen might have a Dread Power that could benefit you, but that's getting into particulars that don't have much to do with being a Huntsman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T12:01:03-07:00","id":1395413,"title":"","content":"Huntsmen aren't True Fey; they predate the True Fey in Arcadia. Some were bargained with and others coerced into service. Some may run free and others may operate in a mercenary capacity, presumably, but the ones that get sent out to hunt have been locked into service by removing their heart and replacing it with the will of their master.<br /> <br /> A mortal Bastion contains the Huntsman's heart. If removed, the Huntsman can't enter the physical realm. Discovering this detail would be a pretty difficult Mystery on its own, I imagine, but it unlocks a handful of interesting possibilities. Presumably, that heart is Connected to the Huntsman, so summoning one via Sympathy of its heart should be possible. This would obviously violate the rules of the magic keeping the Bastion hidden from the Huntsman and arguably qualify as forcing them to violate the will of their master. Clash of Wills would be involved and one could argue the Bastion protections would always go in the Gentry's favor. That doesn't prevent a dreamwalker from removing the heart from the Bastion, first, however, and avoiding that matter.<br /> <br /> Summoning an untitled Huntsman from Arcadia seems like it would either require a very special Mystery or visiting and making a deal or both. Not convinced there should be such an option. Mage being what it is, pulling out the heart and replacing it probably should be possible, but would be seriously wacky magic---well into homebrew territory. I'd probably consider that Fate-dominated soul manipulation, so Death and Fate would figure prominently. (Bare minimum of 4th dots for that, too, unless you assume that Hunsman Hearts are easy to extract and a normal part of what they are.)<br /> <br /> (Described as it is, the &quot;undeveloped lands&quot; in Arcadia of 2e sound and act a whole lot like a Lower Depth. Even with the True Fey presence, Arcadia fits that motif rather well, what with the hunger for mortal dreams. That could be an interesting theme to play with.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}